  - THE EQUIPMENT IS RUE''S AND IT IS AMERICAN, which reads oddly on an NGR
    character and is left alone deliberately. The JA-11, the Northern Gun
    pistols and the Wilk''s are what "create the character as usual" resolves
    to; substituting Triax weapons would be inventing a list the book does not
    print, and this book''s own weapon rows are not imported yet. Revisit when
    the gear batch lands.
  - LANGUAGE IS THE ONE PLACE THIS ROW DIFFERS FROM THE JUICER, and the
    difference is a choice OFFERED rather than a bonus granted: the two
    languages of choice may be taken as `Language: Euro`, which the Juicer''s
    own list does not offer because that row predates the Euro skill. Native
    Tongue is left at the Juicer''s 92% and named as Euro in its note for a
    character raised in the NGR. Nothing else is altered.
  - JAEP AND THE DESIGNER DRUGS ARE NOT THIS CLASS AND ARE NOT IMPORTED.
    Printed 175-178 carries the Juicer Augmentation Enhancement Program - four
    enhancement categories with bonuses and market costs of 125,000, 85,000,
    85,000 and 95,000 credits - and six designer drugs with per-dose costs.
    They are open to other O.C.C.s and explicitly closed to this one. They are
    also candidate GEAR rows that the survey''s extraction plan does not list:
    its gear pass covers printed 34-38, 141-154, 205 and 210-214, and none of
    175-178. Recorded in the queue for whoever takes the gear batch.
  - The detoxification tables, the non-human Juicer rules and the Juicer''s
