# Euro-Juicer

## Lore

Juicer technology was originally developed by pre-Rifts German chemical companies, and it flourishes in Rifts Earth and in the New German Republic. Chemical augmentation is not illegal in the NGR - but it is not used by the military or by Triax, both of which rely heavily on bionics and robotics, and it is not encouraged by the government. Most Euro-Juicers are adventurers, explorers, mercenaries or assassins for hire. Few are active soldiers in the NGR military or in law enforcement.

The character is a Juicer in every mechanical respect. The same creation considerations, conditions, skills, bonuses and penalties described for the Rifts Juicer apply to the NGR/European Juicer - the book says to create the character as usual, and its experience table on printed 224 is the Juicer''s own, reprinted.

## A Drug Prevalent Society

The NGR and many European communities have access to drugs and other juicer-like augmentation. Even though these are legal and available on the streets, especially in the industrial cities, they are neither safe nor desirable: drug dependency is dangerous, addictive, has debilitating side effects, and can cause permanent mental or physical damage. The NGR government spends a great deal of money on anti-drug advertising and rehabilitation clinics, the average citizen has been taught the hazards, and 86% avoid it entirely. Drug use for recreation, for quick boosts, and Juicer technology itself all flourish anyway - especially among mercenaries, city rats, bandits, foreign armies and adventurers.

## JAEP, and why it is closed to this class

"Jape", the Juicer Augmentation Enhancement Program, is a full chemical system similar to the Juicer''s - an internal bio-comp and a drug injection collar - that is less addictive, has fewer side effects and is far less lethal, because it is narrowly focused on one area of enhancement rather than raising everything at once. Any human character from any O.C.C. **except** Juicer, Robot or Borg may use it, which excludes this class by definition. It is not recommended for characters using bio-wizardry augmentation or M.O.M. implants, nor for psionics or alien life forms.

The recommended safe use is three months on, three months clean. Only one JAEP may run at a time: two at once causes an overdose, and the G.M. rolls 1D4 of cardiac arrest, stroke, convulsions with paralysis, or permanent brain damage. Continuous use past six months is addictive, and a JAEP addict''s life expectancy falls to 45+1D6 years against a normal NGR citizen''s 80. A Juicer, by contrast, usually dies within a decade of augmentation. The programme has only existed for ten years, which is not long enough to know the real long-term dangers.

## GM Notes

Detoxification, the permanent side-effect table, the year-by-year detox success percentages and the non-human Juicer rules are not repeated here. They are the Juicer''s, and they are on the `juicer` class. Triax printed 175 adds none of its own.

Every mechanical block on this class is a copy of the Juicer''s, taken on 2026-09-06. If the Juicer is corrected, correct this too - nothing links them. See `BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md` F25.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'euro-juicer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'euro-juicer';

